1
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:23,272
"Get up, we're not dragging you."

2
00:00:24,982 --> 00:00:26,025
"You heard him, get in there."

3
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:35,117
- "Where do you want to put him?"
- "Right there."

4
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:46,837
Please.

5
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:49,590
I won't say anything.

6
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:52,552
What are you waiting for?

7
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:57,181
No. No. No!

8
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:20,413
Charles.

9
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:24,083
- A word when you're finished.
- Yes, Mr. Volker.

10
00:01:27,211 --> 00:01:29,714
I'm on my way now.
The reservation's at 8.

11
00:01:30,506 --> 00:01:31,549
Come on, grab his feet.

12
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:37,888
- "Got it."
- Man, he's heavy.

13
00:01:38,931 --> 00:01:39,974
You've got the light end.

14
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:43,144
I'm trying, I'm trying
to get him in there...

15
00:01:50,901 --> 00:01:53,362
All right. Let's get out of here.

16
00:01:55,489 --> 00:01:57,825
- Listen, you around tomorrow?
- Yeah, why?

17
00:01:58,826 --> 00:01:59,910
Might have another job for you.

18
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:06,500
Wait. You hear that?

19
00:02:08,753 --> 00:02:11,005
Hello? Someone there?

20
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:22,183
Come out of there.

21
00:02:28,981 --> 00:02:30,024
What do we do?

22
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:34,111
No choice. He's a witness.

23
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:39,950
Take care of it.

24
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:54,715
What've we got?

25
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:58,135
Victim's male, 30s.
Still working to ID him.

26
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,681
Based on decomp, coroner thinks
he's been dead two months.

27
00:03:01,972 --> 00:03:03,891
Oakland P.D. says
that's when the building was boarded up.

28
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:05,685
Cause of death?

29
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,729
Because of marks on the victim's neck,
the coroner's thinking strangulation.

30
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:12,566
- Dried blood?
- Looks like.

31
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:15,736
So, the victim was killed here,
then moved there?

32
00:03:15,861 --> 00:03:18,698
Yes, but no drag marks.
And he looks to be at least 200 pounds.

33
00:03:20,032 --> 00:03:21,158
Think there's a second killer?

34
00:03:21,617 --> 00:03:23,953
Big guy like that?
Be tough to carry on your own.

35
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:27,123
Rigsby, did anyone else
have access to this building?

36
00:03:27,289 --> 00:03:30,418
Not since it was boarded up. Oakland
P.D. say there was no sign of forced entry

37
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,877
when the demo crew found the body.

38
00:03:33,629 --> 00:03:34,672
Excuse me a minute.

39
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,599
It's a remote-controlled car.

40
00:03:48,185 --> 00:03:51,272
I found it just there.
It's odd, don't you think?

41
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:55,025
Okay, have an ID on the victim.
His name is Horatio Jones.

42
00:03:55,484 --> 00:03:57,069
- Horatio Jones?
- Yeah. You know him?

43
00:03:57,445 --> 00:03:58,487
I know of him.

44
00:03:59,196 --> 00:04:03,868
Horatio Jones, he was a geologist for an
energy company owned by Tommy Volker.

45
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:07,455
He was set to testify before a grand jury
against Volker two months ago.

46
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,622
And then he disappeared.

47
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:12,960
I always thought Volker was behind it,
but now I know it.

48
00:04:14,628 --> 00:04:15,671
Volker did this.

49
00:04:33,929 --> 00:04:35,889
The coroner investigator found tissue
under the victim's fingernails.

50
00:04:36,098 --> 00:04:37,141
It's headed to the lab.

51
00:04:37,266 --> 00:04:40,477
Good, make sure the M.E. gets me the results
from the autopsy as soon as possible.

52
00:04:40,602 --> 00:04:42,146
- I wanna move quickly on this.
- Yes, boss.

53
00:04:45,566 --> 00:04:49,069
{\an8}Volker wouldn't have killed Jones himself.
He never gets his hands dirty.

54
00:04:49,194 --> 00:04:50,696
{\an8}I'm thinking it was Charles Milk.

55
00:04:50,821 --> 00:04:54,616
{\an8}That would be helpful if only Charles Milk
hadn't been killed last week.

56
00:04:54,867 --> 00:04:58,579
{\an8}Forensics thinks they might have something.
It might even tie Volker to the crime.

57
00:04:58,704 --> 00:04:59,830
You think he was here?

58
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:02,916
{\an8}He gets off on this,
watching his victims die.

59
00:05:03,584 --> 00:05:06,462
{\an8}- I need Volker's DNA.
- Well, just ask him for it.

60
00:05:06,712 --> 00:05:08,464
- You think he'd give it to me?
- Yes.

61
00:05:08,797 --> 00:05:11,800
Volker's arrogant. He likes
to pretend he has nothing to hide.

62
00:05:11,925 --> 00:05:15,763
{\an8}Lisbon, answer me this,
who would leave this here?

63
00:05:16,930 --> 00:05:18,015
{\an8}A small child?

64
00:05:18,140 --> 00:05:20,225
{\an8}- Yeah, like 9 or 10 years old.
- Something like that.

65
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:22,060
{\an8}- Most likely a boy.
- Yeah.

66
00:05:22,311 --> 00:05:24,104
{\an8}A boy that hasn't been here
in two months.

67
00:05:24,229 --> 00:05:26,690
{\an8}Because that's when Oakland P.D.
said this place was boarded up.

68
00:05:26,857 --> 00:05:27,900
What are you getting at?

69
00:05:28,025 --> 00:05:31,320
{\an8}Well, no self-respecting kid
would leave this behind.

70
00:05:31,862 --> 00:05:33,614
Other than the dust,
it's practically brand new.

71
00:05:33,739 --> 00:05:36,658
{\an8}Which means he left it
for an urgent reason.

72
00:05:38,285 --> 00:05:40,996
- He witnessed the murder.
- Or it's just a toy car.

73
00:05:41,622 --> 00:05:43,040
It's thin, I know.

74
00:05:43,165 --> 00:05:45,292
{\an8}If there was a boy
and if he witnessed a murder

75
00:05:45,417 --> 00:05:48,670
{\an8}- he would've come forward months ago.
- Not if the killer found him.

76
00:05:49,046 --> 00:05:52,883
{\an8}If that was the case, we would've found
his body with Jones', don't you think?

77
00:05:53,008 --> 00:05:55,969
{\an8}- Yes, one would think.
- I'm gonna go talk to Volker.

78
00:05:56,470 --> 00:05:59,223
{\an8}You go and look into this theoretical kid.

79
00:05:59,348 --> 00:06:02,059
- You don't want me to come with you?
- No. I'll meet you back at the office.

80
00:06:03,227 --> 00:06:04,269
{\an8}Fine.

81
00:06:04,937 --> 00:06:07,272
{\an8}The maiden voyage
of Volker Intergalactic...

82
00:06:07,397 --> 00:06:09,817
{\an8}has been set, it's been publicized,
we're not postponing.

83
00:06:10,984 --> 00:06:12,694
Can't find a solution, find another job.

84
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,825
Agent Lisbon

85
00:06:18,992 --> 00:06:21,036
{\an8}I have to admit,
I'm surprised to see you again.

86
00:06:22,329 --> 00:06:24,748
{\an8}Surprised but pleased.

87
00:06:26,041 --> 00:06:28,794
- We found your missing employee.
- Employee?

88
00:06:29,127 --> 00:06:32,631
{\an8}Horatio Jones.
He's been missing for two months.

89
00:06:32,756 --> 00:06:35,634
{\an8}He worked for a company you own,
VNX Energy.

90
00:06:36,593 --> 00:06:40,097
{\an8}We found his body
earlier this morning. Murdered.

91
00:06:41,056 --> 00:06:42,099
I'm sorry to hear that.

92
00:06:42,891 --> 00:06:47,145
{\an8}- Did you know him?
- I have thousands of employees, agent.

93
00:06:47,646 --> 00:06:50,232
{\an8}Unfortunately,
I don't get to meet each one.

94
00:06:50,983 --> 00:06:52,025
{\an8}Well, that's odd

95
00:06:52,150 --> 00:06:55,445
{\an8}because Jones was deposed in
a grand-jury inquiry into your activities.

96
00:06:55,946 --> 00:06:56,989
I said I didn't know him.

97
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:00,909
{\an8}Not that I didn't know about him.

98
00:07:03,287 --> 00:07:04,997
{\an8}Jones was working in the Amazon...

99
00:07:05,706 --> 00:07:08,959
as part of a geothermal energy project
I was developing.

100
00:07:09,084 --> 00:07:10,586
{\an8}A project that ran into problems

101
00:07:10,711 --> 00:07:13,255
{\an8}when a local
tribe claimed the site as sacred ground.

102
00:07:13,797 --> 00:07:17,092
Weeks later, the tribe was found dead
in a mass grave.

103
00:07:17,426 --> 00:07:20,095
{\an8}This again.
I see we've come full circle.

104
00:07:20,345 --> 00:07:21,930
You were implicated in a crime.

105
00:07:22,097 --> 00:07:25,726
In fact, a grand jury was convened
to investigate your involvement.

106
00:07:26,143 --> 00:07:27,519
{\an8}That investigation was dropped.

107
00:07:27,978 --> 00:07:31,565
{\an8}Only after two people who were gonna
testify against you were found dead.

108
00:07:32,024 --> 00:07:34,526
Cassie Flood and Amanda Shaw.
Jones makes three.

109
00:07:34,651 --> 00:07:37,779
Tragic loss,
but again, territory we've covered.

110
00:07:38,155 --> 00:07:41,366
Jones was on his way to turn in evidence
against you when he went missing.

111
00:07:41,491 --> 00:07:45,495
- Excuse me, when he was murdered.
- Do you enjoy this, Agent Lisbon?

112
00:07:48,206 --> 00:07:52,920
{\an8}Wasting your time in this fruitless effort
to persecute me?

113
00:07:54,463 --> 00:07:55,505
Is that really why you're here?

114
00:07:56,381 --> 00:08:00,177
Actually, I came to get a DNA sample.

115
00:08:02,179 --> 00:08:04,556
Unless for some reason
you'd rather not?

116
00:08:07,768 --> 00:08:09,019
And what reason would that be?

117
00:08:30,832 --> 00:08:32,918
I know you had Jones killed.

118
00:08:33,251 --> 00:08:35,045
Just like Cassie Flood
and Amanda Shaw.

119
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:36,922
And this time, I'm gonna prove it.

120
00:08:41,343 --> 00:08:42,552
Best of luck to you, agent.

121
00:08:49,059 --> 00:08:50,102
All right, here it is.

122
00:08:50,268 --> 00:08:53,814
A complete list of children reported
missing two months ago in the Oakland area.

123
00:08:54,189 --> 00:08:56,108
- How many are there?
- Twelve total.

124
00:08:56,692 --> 00:08:57,734
Let's cut that down.

125
00:08:57,859 --> 00:09:00,988
We know we're looking for a boy
between the ages of 9 and 12.

126
00:09:01,154 --> 00:09:02,280
Old enough to be out in the street

127
00:09:02,406 --> 00:09:04,825
but young enough to be playing
with a remote-controlled car.

128
00:09:05,534 --> 00:09:08,370
- Okay. That got us down to five.
- All right.

129
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:11,915
The boy was playing alone
in a bad neighborhood.

130
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:15,252
Probably from a low-income,
single-parent family.

131
00:09:17,129 --> 00:09:20,048
- Two left.
- Which one lived closer to the crime scene?

132
00:09:22,551 --> 00:09:23,593
Marvin Pettigrew.

133
00:09:24,052 --> 00:09:26,221
His home is half a mile
from the warehouse.

134
00:09:27,014 --> 00:09:30,308
Marvin Pettigrew. Thank you.

135
00:09:35,397 --> 00:09:36,440
How'd it go with Volker?

136
00:09:36,857 --> 00:09:39,109
Good. He gave up his DNA
just like you said he would.

137
00:09:39,443 --> 00:09:41,945
- He's behind this, Jane. I know it.
- But?

138
00:09:42,279 --> 00:09:44,031
When grand jury investigation was dropped...

139
00:09:44,156 --> 00:09:47,242
Volker's lawyers had all evidence
and court documents sealed from the case.

140
00:09:47,367 --> 00:09:49,202
Including Jones' deposition.

141
00:09:49,411 --> 00:09:51,747
I think there's something in there
that Volker doesn't want us to know.

142
00:09:52,122 --> 00:09:54,082
- If I could just get my hands on it.
- Why can't you?

143
00:09:55,042 --> 00:09:57,627
They're sealed documents, Jane.
It's against the law.

144
00:09:57,961 --> 00:10:00,630
Well, if you wanna get Volker,
you can't let that stop you.

145
00:10:01,465 --> 00:10:02,549
What do you suggest?

146
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:06,303
Ardiles is a deputy DA.
He's gonna have the deposition.

147
00:10:06,428 --> 00:10:08,472
Ardiles is not gonna stick
his neck out for me.

148
00:10:08,597 --> 00:10:10,682
Of course not. He's a smart lawyer.

149
00:10:11,016 --> 00:10:14,019
You have to get something on him
that will make him help you.

150
00:10:15,062 --> 00:10:18,065
- Blackmail the deputy district attorney?
- Sure, why not?

151
00:10:22,027 --> 00:10:25,322
- How could I get dirt on Ardiles?
- Ask yourself this

152
00:10:26,531 --> 00:10:28,909
Who makes it their business
to know everyone else's?

153
00:10:33,914 --> 00:10:36,083
Well, I have to hand it to you.
You get right to the point.

154
00:10:37,125 --> 00:10:38,168
It's actually refreshing.

155
00:10:39,169 --> 00:10:40,754
- Will you help me?
- Maybe.

156
00:10:41,713 --> 00:10:44,549
- What's your problem with Ardiles?
- I don't have a problem with Ardiles.

157
00:10:44,674 --> 00:10:46,051
- It's about a case.
- What case?

158
00:10:47,052 --> 00:10:49,846
- I can't tell you.
- I don't know, Teresa.

159
00:10:50,764 --> 00:10:53,100
Brenda, I'll owe you.

160
00:10:54,810 --> 00:10:57,813
One day you will need a favor,
and I will owe you.

161
00:11:02,818 --> 00:11:04,694
I can't give you any specific details.

162
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:08,573
But if you were to mention
the Ferland case to Ardiles...

163
00:11:08,698 --> 00:11:10,450
you might find him more compliant
to your request.

164
00:11:11,201 --> 00:11:12,744
- Thank you.
- Teresa.

165
00:11:14,329 --> 00:11:15,705
This is murky water you're swimming in.

166
00:11:16,039 --> 00:11:18,416
Whatever this is about,
I hope it's worth it.

167
00:11:18,959 --> 00:11:20,001
It is.

168
00:11:25,048 --> 00:11:28,760
{\an8}Marvin went missing 61 days ago.

169
00:11:30,846 --> 00:11:34,558
His teacher watched him leave the school.
That's the last time anyone saw him.

170
00:11:36,309 --> 00:11:40,522
I found a toy car at an abandoned
warehouse. I just wanted to...

171
00:11:41,815 --> 00:11:44,860
I just wanted to know if it...
If it belonged to your son.

172
00:11:55,662 --> 00:11:56,955
That was his birthday present.

173
00:11:58,915 --> 00:12:00,333
He'd wanted it for months.

174
00:12:04,921 --> 00:12:06,423
You say you found this at a warehouse?

175
00:12:07,299 --> 00:12:10,677
- About half a mile from here.
- I know the one.

176
00:12:12,846 --> 00:12:16,183
Marvin used to walk past it
on his way home from school.

177
00:12:16,975 --> 00:12:18,351
I told him not to play there.

178
00:12:21,938 --> 00:12:26,234
That warehouse was...
was the scene of a crime.

179
00:12:30,155 --> 00:12:31,573
A man was found murdered there.

180
00:12:36,119 --> 00:12:37,162
Mr. Jane...

181
00:12:39,456 --> 00:12:40,624
is my boy dead?

182
00:12:44,044 --> 00:12:46,171
I don't know. I don't know.

183
00:12:53,011 --> 00:12:54,971
- Ardiles.
- Lisbon.

184
00:12:55,388 --> 00:12:56,431
Thanks for coming by.

185
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:59,226
- Can I get you something to drink?
- A drink? No.

186
00:12:59,392 --> 00:13:03,230
I... I gotta be back in court in 20 minutes,
so, what's this about?

187
00:13:03,438 --> 00:13:07,192
Two months ago there was a grand-jury
investigation into Tommy Volker.

188
00:13:07,442 --> 00:13:11,529
A witness was deposed by the name of
Horatio Jones. The documents were sealed.

189
00:13:12,906 --> 00:13:13,949
And?

190
00:13:15,617 --> 00:13:16,743
I need that deposition.

191
00:13:17,619 --> 00:13:20,205
The deposition was sealed
by a grand jury.

192
00:13:21,331 --> 00:13:23,667
Two witnesses against Volker
have been found dead.

193
00:13:23,917 --> 00:13:25,168
We found a third this morning.

194
00:13:25,293 --> 00:13:28,046
Yeah, I'm sorry to hear about that,
but I'm not gonna break the law for you.

195
00:13:28,171 --> 00:13:30,090
I understand you're under a lot of pressure.

196
00:13:30,215 --> 00:13:32,425
Maybe it's the job,
maybe it's the Ferland case.

197
00:13:36,096 --> 00:13:39,557
- What do you know about the Ferland case?
- Not a lot. Now.

198
00:13:40,308 --> 00:13:42,435
But I will if you don't get me
those depositions.

199
00:13:47,148 --> 00:13:49,442
Okay. You'll have them within an hour.

200
00:14:07,335 --> 00:14:08,461
Hey, boss. How's it coming?

201
00:14:09,462 --> 00:14:11,923
Nothing so far. We already know
everything that's here.

202
00:14:12,048 --> 00:14:13,842
- What about you? Did you find anything?
- Maybe.

203
00:14:14,092 --> 00:14:17,762
In the deposition, Jones mentions that
a friend from college visited him in Brazil.

204
00:14:18,596 --> 00:14:22,559
Annabelle Sugalski. It's a shot in the dark,
but maybe Jones talked to her about Volker.

205
00:14:23,393 --> 00:14:24,477
- Bring her in.
- Okay.

206
00:14:27,856 --> 00:14:30,191
I knew Horatio worked for Volker,
but that's it.

207
00:14:30,942 --> 00:14:32,235
He never really said much about him.

208
00:14:32,694 --> 00:14:34,404
Did he mention work?
The project he was on?

209
00:14:35,363 --> 00:14:36,406
"Briefly."

210
00:14:37,032 --> 00:14:39,367
- "It was an energy project, right?"
- Yeah. In the Amazon.

211
00:14:39,826 --> 00:14:41,494
All he said
was they were having problems.

212
00:14:42,078 --> 00:14:43,621
Did Horatio say anything
about a mass killing?

213
00:14:44,539 --> 00:14:46,833
- No.
- You're certain?

214
00:14:48,335 --> 00:14:49,377
Yeah. Of course.

215
00:14:53,048 --> 00:14:54,841
Anabelle, has anyone else talked
to you about this?

216
00:14:55,342 --> 00:14:56,384
What do you mean?

217
00:14:56,593 --> 00:14:58,595
Has anyone asked you
to withhold information from us?

218
00:14:59,721 --> 00:15:00,764
God, no.

219
00:15:02,390 --> 00:15:05,435
Look, I was in Brazil on vacation.

220
00:15:06,061 --> 00:15:09,064
Horatio and I only saw each other
a couple times. Dinner, drinks, that's it.

221
00:15:09,856 --> 00:15:12,525
"Sorry I can't help you. I wish I could."

222
00:15:14,527 --> 00:15:16,196
So, what did you tell them?

223
00:15:17,238 --> 00:15:19,032
Exactly what you told me to.
Nothing.

224
00:15:20,784 --> 00:15:23,745
- And they believed you?
- Every word.

225
00:15:28,249 --> 00:15:30,752
And the voice mail Jones left for you?

226
00:15:33,463 --> 00:15:34,881
I deleted it.
You can check my phone.

227
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:43,932
You know, you're quite the liability.

228
00:15:47,352 --> 00:15:48,686
And I hate liabilities.

229
00:15:53,358 --> 00:15:54,609
But I like you, Annabelle.

230
00:15:58,488 --> 00:16:00,198
And I would hate for something
to happen to you.

231
00:16:01,491 --> 00:16:03,326
Please, I won't tell anyone, I promise.

232
00:16:05,954 --> 00:16:08,206
I'm leaving the country tonight.
You'll never see me again.

233
00:16:10,875 --> 00:16:11,918
That's a shame.

234
00:16:20,718 --> 00:16:21,761
Good night.

235
00:16:44,742 --> 00:16:47,078
Hey. Any luck finding the kid?

236
00:16:47,662 --> 00:16:49,998
We gave his name and photo
to local police...

237
00:16:50,123 --> 00:16:52,333
and the FBI's Department
of Missing Persons.

238
00:16:52,459 --> 00:16:55,253
But it's like finding a needle
in a stack of needles.

239
00:16:55,503 --> 00:16:57,589
- I heard you talked to his mother.
- Yes.

240
00:16:57,839 --> 00:17:00,300
She thinks the worst.
Hard not to agree with her.

241
00:17:01,301 --> 00:17:03,845
What about you?
Burning the midnight oil, I see.

242
00:17:04,804 --> 00:17:06,139
There's gotta be something here.

243
00:17:09,267 --> 00:17:12,270
Jane, Amanda Shaw was my witness.

244
00:17:12,687 --> 00:17:16,399
I gave her my word that I'd protect her,
and Volker had her killed.

245
00:17:28,036 --> 00:17:29,078
Done with this?

246
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:32,123
Good.

247
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:44,900
Morning, boss. I just got word. Annabelle
Sugalski left the country last night.

248
00:17:45,026 --> 00:17:47,820
- Flew out on a red-eye to London.
- He got to her. Damn it.

249
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:52,992
In Jones' deposition, he said he gave
evidence against Volker in written reports.

250
00:17:53,117 --> 00:17:54,493
I saw that, but none were found.

251
00:17:54,702 --> 00:17:57,622
- What if Jones gave them to his employer?
- VNX Energy?

252
00:17:57,788 --> 00:17:58,831
Let's go check it out.

253
00:18:07,006 --> 00:18:09,342
That was the M.E.
with the test results from the autopsy.

254
00:18:09,884 --> 00:18:12,678
DNA identifies Charles Milk
as one of the killers.

255
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:15,848
The M.E. also found a second DNA.
A strand of hair.

256
00:18:16,474 --> 00:18:18,643
I was hoping it was Volker,
but no such luck.

257
00:18:18,809 --> 00:18:22,605
- No. Volker's far too careful.
- So far no match in the federal database.

258
00:18:23,064 --> 00:18:25,149
It does prove that there was another person
present at the murder.

259
00:18:25,775 --> 00:18:27,193
Question is, who was it?

260
00:18:37,161 --> 00:18:38,913
Hi, we need to speak with the manager.

261
00:18:39,330 --> 00:18:41,624
- Is everything all right?
- Just have a few questions.

262
00:18:42,375 --> 00:18:43,417
Let me get him.

263
00:18:54,595 --> 00:18:56,138
- Come on.
- We're leaving?

264
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:01,727
Volker has been a step ahead of us
this entire time.

265
00:19:01,852 --> 00:19:03,688
He finds out
we're looking into VNX Energy...

266
00:19:03,813 --> 00:19:06,148
any chance we have
of finding that evidence is gone.

267
00:19:08,109 --> 00:19:10,653
"It rained for a week, night and day."

268
00:19:11,612 --> 00:19:14,740
"During the week, the fish were
in their houses keeping nice and warm."

269
00:19:15,866 --> 00:19:19,412
"When it finally stopped raining,
all the fish went outside..."

270
00:19:19,537 --> 00:19:22,415
"and saw Spike in a small puddle
growing gills."

271
00:19:22,998 --> 00:19:25,167
"The fish yelled,
'How's life in the water?'"

272
00:19:25,501 --> 00:19:27,795
"And Spike yelled back,
'Great! Come on in!'"

273
00:19:28,587 --> 00:19:32,091
"And that is why fish live in water."

274
00:19:33,676 --> 00:19:34,719
The end.

275
00:19:36,637 --> 00:19:39,640
What do we say to Mr. Volker
for sharing his time with us?

276
00:19:40,057 --> 00:19:43,853
- Thank you, Mr. Volker.
- You're very welcome.

277
00:19:45,104 --> 00:19:46,355
Thank you. See you again.

278
00:19:48,065 --> 00:19:49,108
Bye, kids.

279
00:19:52,611 --> 00:19:53,654
Uh, Mr. Volker.

280
00:19:54,822 --> 00:20:00,578
- Patrick Jane. I work with Teresa Lisbon.
- Ah, yes, Mr. Jane, nice to meet you.

281
00:20:01,328 --> 00:20:02,663
Any friend of Teresa's.

282
00:20:03,456 --> 00:20:06,459
- She's a fascinating woman, isn't she?
- Certainly.

283
00:20:07,251 --> 00:20:11,088
Well, that was impressive. Not only are you
a super-successful businessman...

284
00:20:11,213 --> 00:20:13,507
but you're quite the vivid storyteller.

285
00:20:13,632 --> 00:20:17,178
For a moment, I was splashing around in
that puddle with Spike, growing some gills.

286
00:20:19,805 --> 00:20:22,433
- Was there something you needed?
- Need, no.

287
00:20:22,808 --> 00:20:25,436
I just wanted to meet you
while I have the chance.

288
00:20:26,645 --> 00:20:30,107
- Are you going somewhere?
- No. But you are.

289
00:20:30,566 --> 00:20:32,902
After your arrest,
things are bound to get hectic.

290
00:20:33,027 --> 00:20:35,863
And I probably won't have the chance
to introduce myself, so here I am.

291
00:20:36,238 --> 00:20:37,281
Very droll.

292
00:20:37,865 --> 00:20:41,243
But you and I both know
that I'm not gonna be arrested.

293
00:20:45,873 --> 00:20:46,916
You sure about that?

294
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,965
- Are you finished?
- Yes.

295
00:21:09,522 --> 00:21:12,691
"Gray suit,
salt-and-pepper hair, 6 feet tall."

296
00:21:12,817 --> 00:21:15,110
- "He's coming out now."
- All right, got him.

297
00:21:30,251 --> 00:21:33,712
- Good evening, Agent Lisbon.
- I'm sorry to bother you, Your Honor.

298
00:21:33,838 --> 00:21:34,964
All right. Let's see it.

299
00:21:38,008 --> 00:21:40,261
- So how are Emily and Ruth?
- They're good.

300
00:21:40,719 --> 00:21:43,556
- Emily's at Santa Cruz, right?
- Santa Clara.

301
00:21:44,181 --> 00:21:45,224
Yeah...

302
00:21:46,141 --> 00:21:47,184
Is this all you have?

303
00:21:48,352 --> 00:21:51,814
Yes, but it's clear that Tommy Volker
is a very dangerous man.

304
00:21:52,022 --> 00:21:53,983
Well, that may be true, Agent Lisbon.

305
00:21:54,358 --> 00:21:56,819
- But this is not enough for a warrant.
- Your Honor, if you just...

306
00:21:56,944 --> 00:22:00,447
You have no proof that evidence against
Mr. Volker is inside VNX Industries.

307
00:22:00,573 --> 00:22:01,615
I'm sorry, I can't sign it.

308
00:22:03,075 --> 00:22:04,118
Yes, Your Honor.

309
00:22:05,369 --> 00:22:06,412
Good evening.

310
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:24,305
- Hello, Lisbon, what's up?
- I just left Judge Davis' office.

311
00:22:24,430 --> 00:22:27,683
- She won't sign the VNX warrant.
- Are you asking me what I would do?

312
00:22:28,225 --> 00:22:33,230
- No. I already know the answer.
- Okay. Good night, Lisbon.

313
00:22:40,195 --> 00:22:42,698
I am sorry. But that was my office.
We got it.

314
00:22:42,823 --> 00:22:44,992
Confirmation that there's evidence
against Thommas Volker

315
00:22:45,117 --> 00:22:48,412
- inside the VNX Energy offices.
- What kind of confirmation?

316
00:22:48,537 --> 00:22:50,581
It's a coworker of Jones'
who still works at the company.

317
00:22:50,706 --> 00:22:53,459
I can get you a transcript of the
questioning first thing in the morning.

318
00:22:53,584 --> 00:22:55,002
But time is of the essence.

319
00:23:16,607 --> 00:23:17,650
Got something.

320
00:23:20,027 --> 00:23:22,863
Don Clyde, 48, no priors.

321
00:23:23,906 --> 00:23:26,367
Looks like he was a ward on the state
when his mother died.

322
00:23:26,742 --> 00:23:29,954
He spent the last six years as a private
security contractor in the Middle East.

323
00:23:30,245 --> 00:23:32,456
A mercenary.
Does he have any family?

324
00:23:33,916 --> 00:23:35,918
Yep, younger brother, John Clyde.

325
00:23:36,543 --> 00:23:38,462
But he's serving two years
in Lompoc on a battery charge.

326
00:23:41,465 --> 00:23:43,759
All right, I want this to be careful
and methodical.

327
00:23:43,884 --> 00:23:45,386
I don't want anything
to slip through the cracks.

328
00:23:47,388 --> 00:23:48,430
Oh, no.

329
00:23:54,019 --> 00:23:55,562
- Volker.
- How did he know?

330
00:23:57,231 --> 00:23:59,608
- I'll take the two on the end.
- I'll take this one.

331
00:24:18,377 --> 00:24:19,461
I'm looking for Agent Lisbon.

332
00:24:25,134 --> 00:24:26,176
Boss.

333
00:24:29,221 --> 00:24:30,264
What are you doing here?

334
00:24:31,348 --> 00:24:32,391
Such hostility.

335
00:24:33,851 --> 00:24:36,645
- And here I thought we were mending fences.
- Answer the question.

336
00:24:38,605 --> 00:24:41,567
I came to ask you
to drop this ridiculous investigation.

337
00:24:42,985 --> 00:24:45,863
I hate to see an officer of the law
humiliated like this.

338
00:24:47,448 --> 00:24:50,451
- Cho, will you show Mr. Volker out of here?
- Gladly.

339
00:24:52,327 --> 00:24:53,579
I'm only looking out
for your best interest.

340
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:56,123
No, you're not.

341
00:24:58,876 --> 00:25:01,420
You want us to think
that you're gloating, but you're not.

342
00:25:02,755 --> 00:25:05,758
- You're afraid. Yeah
- Heh. Afraid?

343
00:25:07,092 --> 00:25:09,344
Well, this certainly
is a strange way of showing it.

344
00:25:09,636 --> 00:25:10,971
I can see right through you.

345
00:25:12,181 --> 00:25:15,726
We were close, searching
your offices like that. Too close.

346
00:25:16,727 --> 00:25:19,271
You want us to think that you're in control,
that you're untouchable.

347
00:25:19,605 --> 00:25:20,647
But you're not.

348
00:25:21,774 --> 00:25:22,816
You're afraid of us.

349
00:25:25,152 --> 00:25:26,195
And you should be.

350
00:25:41,783 --> 00:25:44,619
So you think Don Clyde
helped kill Horatio Jones?

351
00:25:44,745 --> 00:25:47,998
Yeah, I'm sure of it.
Well, fairly sure of it.

352
00:25:48,582 --> 00:25:50,625
- But we have no proof.
- Correct.

353
00:25:52,127 --> 00:25:54,004
So if we bring him in,
we won't have any leverage.

354
00:25:54,129 --> 00:25:56,923
But if we keep digging, Volker might
find out and make him disappear.

355
00:25:57,549 --> 00:26:00,177
So bring him in and fake the leverage.

356
00:26:10,729 --> 00:26:11,897
Get out. Hands in the air.

357
00:26:12,189 --> 00:26:13,857
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.
- Turn around.

358
00:26:14,608 --> 00:26:17,194
- Whoa.
- Turn around. Do it now.

359
00:26:17,944 --> 00:26:18,987
What's going on here?

360
00:26:20,405 --> 00:26:21,448
Come on, what is this?

361
00:26:22,074 --> 00:26:23,116
- What's going on?
- Get in the car.

362
00:26:23,742 --> 00:26:24,785
Oh, man.

363
00:26:27,662 --> 00:26:28,705
What'd I do?

364
00:26:45,514 --> 00:26:47,516
We know you work for Tommy Volker.

365
00:26:47,641 --> 00:26:51,603
You were working for him the day that you
and Charles Milk murdered Horatio Jones.

366
00:26:52,562 --> 00:26:55,524
- Volker was there, wasn't he?
- I don't know what you're talking about.

367
00:26:56,233 --> 00:26:58,652
We can help you,
but you're gonna have to work with us.

368
00:27:01,154 --> 00:27:02,322
Something just occurred to me.

369
00:27:04,074 --> 00:27:08,328
You haven't asked for a lawyer. Why?
A man in your vocation...

370
00:27:08,453 --> 00:27:11,540
- wouldn't that be second nature?
- Only guilty men need lawyers.

371
00:27:13,125 --> 00:27:14,543
Nice try. But that's not it.

372
00:27:15,168 --> 00:27:18,004
We'll go back to that.
I just wanna run a theory by you.

373
00:27:18,505 --> 00:27:22,217
You see, we know someone
saw you kill Jones.

374
00:27:23,552 --> 00:27:24,594
A boy.

375
00:27:27,097 --> 00:27:29,141
Marvin, he saw what you did, didn't he?

376
00:27:31,476 --> 00:27:32,519
Yes.

377
00:27:33,812 --> 00:27:34,855
So you killed him.

378
00:27:40,110 --> 00:27:41,736
I would never kill a child.

379
00:27:43,864 --> 00:27:45,490
No. You wouldn't.

380
00:27:46,616 --> 00:27:48,869
You didn't choose this life.
You were forced into it.

381
00:27:48,994 --> 00:27:51,997
A ward of the state with no options.
You don't enjoy what you do.

382
00:27:52,289 --> 00:27:56,334
And you're not a sociopath
like Volker or Charles Milk.

383
00:27:57,252 --> 00:27:59,212
So you let one of them kill the boy.

384
00:28:01,923 --> 00:28:02,966
- No.
- No?

385
00:28:05,802 --> 00:28:06,845
Unless...

386
00:28:08,722 --> 00:28:10,056
Unless he's still alive.

387
00:28:13,393 --> 00:28:14,436
He is, isn't he?

388
00:28:15,937 --> 00:28:16,980
You couldn't kill him.

389
00:28:17,731 --> 00:28:21,735
But you couldn't let a witness
to a murder that you committed go free.

390
00:28:22,819 --> 00:28:25,488
So you took him. You gave him up
to someone you trusted.

391
00:28:26,114 --> 00:28:29,701
The boy would be safe and any talk
of murder would fall on deaf ears.

392
00:28:32,495 --> 00:28:36,416
What'd you do with him, Clyde?
Where is Marvin Pettigrew?

393
00:28:40,420 --> 00:28:45,550
- If I talk, I'm a dead man.
- If you don't, it's just a matter of time.

394
00:28:46,426 --> 00:28:48,053
Think about your situation here.

395
00:28:48,929 --> 00:28:51,765
We are gonna start actively looking
for Marvin Pettigrew.

396
00:28:52,724 --> 00:28:54,809
When Volker finds out
you let a witness go...

397
00:28:54,935 --> 00:28:58,271
a witness that could tie him to the Jones
murder, what do you think he's gonna do?

398
00:28:58,688 --> 00:29:00,357
You know his methods
better than anyone.

399
00:29:04,569 --> 00:29:05,612
I'm not saying another word.

400
00:29:09,991 --> 00:29:11,826
- So, what now?
- We have to let him go.

401
00:29:12,244 --> 00:29:14,037
Volker will go after him,
just like you said he would.

402
00:29:14,162 --> 00:29:16,039
Yes, but not today.
Volker's not that good.

403
00:29:16,623 --> 00:29:18,750
- Meanwhile Clyde'll lead us to Marvin.
- Exactly.

404
00:29:18,875 --> 00:29:19,918
Cold. I like it.

405
00:29:21,586 --> 00:29:24,839
Rigsby, I'm releasing Clyde.
Drop him off a couple miles away.

406
00:29:24,965 --> 00:29:27,217
- Volker cannot know he was here.
- Sure thing, boss.

407
00:29:27,801 --> 00:29:29,344
Cho, I need you to tail him.

408
00:29:29,469 --> 00:29:31,763
- Maybe he'll lead us to Marvin Pettigrew.
- You got it.

409
00:29:43,525 --> 00:29:44,609
All right. Get out.

410
00:29:45,860 --> 00:29:49,614
- My apartment's half an hour away.
- Call a cab.

411
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:12,762
Yeah, can I have a cab?

412
00:30:18,977 --> 00:30:20,020
Hey.

413
00:30:20,979 --> 00:30:23,315
- Oh. Is that diet?
- Yeah.

414
00:30:28,028 --> 00:30:29,821
It's like a week old.
Why didn't you tell me?

415
00:30:30,655 --> 00:30:31,698
You didn't ask.

416
00:30:43,043 --> 00:30:44,085
Hello?

417
00:30:44,878 --> 00:30:49,841
- How is Agent Lisbon today?
- I don't know what you're talking about.

418
00:30:53,470 --> 00:30:54,512
Clyde.

419
00:30:56,723 --> 00:30:57,766
You're lying to me.

420
00:30:59,225 --> 00:31:00,268
"You're a dead man."

421
00:31:05,190 --> 00:31:07,901
- What's he doing?
- I don't know.

422
00:31:19,871 --> 00:31:21,081
- No.
- Right there!

423
00:31:21,498 --> 00:31:23,291
- Oh, no.
- What is that?

424
00:31:25,001 --> 00:31:26,086
You said there was something else?

425
00:31:30,757 --> 00:31:33,551
Yes, but...

426
00:31:38,848 --> 00:31:40,392
There's no need
to be worried about it, Brenda.

427
00:31:43,770 --> 00:31:45,355
- What is it?
- Please don't make me do this.

428
00:31:47,565 --> 00:31:48,608
Make you?

429
00:31:50,443 --> 00:31:52,362
You entered into this relationship
willingly.

430
00:31:52,654 --> 00:31:53,696
Not this.

431
00:31:55,115 --> 00:31:57,909
- I didn't agree to this.
- Give me the envelope.

432
00:32:14,551 --> 00:32:15,593
Who is he?

433
00:32:15,718 --> 00:32:17,554
They think he's a witness to Jones' murder.

434
00:32:24,310 --> 00:32:25,854
- Where is he?
- I don't know.

435
00:32:32,777 --> 00:32:37,365
- I said, where is he?
- I don't know. I swear.

436
00:32:47,876 --> 00:32:51,129
Mr. Costa. I have a job for you.

437
00:32:57,800 --> 00:32:58,926
Did he say anything?

438
00:32:59,051 --> 00:33:01,345
No, he made a call, dropped his cell,
and walked into the street.

439
00:33:01,637 --> 00:33:04,015
- Last call was from Volker's office.
- We need to find the boy.

440
00:33:04,223 --> 00:33:05,808
And we need to hurry,
Volker knows about him.

441
00:33:06,184 --> 00:33:08,936
- How? You think Clyde told him?
- Someone's feeding him information.

442
00:33:09,061 --> 00:33:10,146
- Yeah, but who?
- I'm not sure.

443
00:33:10,271 --> 00:33:13,316
But that's how he knew about Annabelle
and the search warrant for VNX energy.

444
00:33:13,441 --> 00:33:14,692
That's how he knew about Clyde.

445
00:33:14,817 --> 00:33:16,861
It's only a matter of time
before he finds Marvin.

446
00:33:22,533 --> 00:33:24,952
Van Pelt, did you get a print out
of Clyde's cell contacts?

447
00:33:25,077 --> 00:33:26,120
Yeah, right here.

448
00:33:26,329 --> 00:33:27,914
All right.
Here's how we gonna do this.

449
00:33:28,122 --> 00:33:31,501
We will split up the list and see if we can
figure out who Clyde left the boy with.

450
00:33:31,626 --> 00:33:33,252
We'll need background checks
on everyone.

451
00:33:33,628 --> 00:33:36,005
It will be someone close to Clyde,
but not immediate family.

452
00:33:36,130 --> 00:33:38,549
A cousin, childhood friend, ex-girlfriend.

453
00:33:38,674 --> 00:33:40,927
Most likely a woman that doesn't have
children of her own...

454
00:33:41,052 --> 00:33:43,304
somewhere between 25 and 50.

455
00:33:43,429 --> 00:33:45,848
- Someone who would want to be a mother.
- Exactly.

456
00:33:45,973 --> 00:33:47,517
All right, we're on a clock. Let's move.

457
00:34:20,049 --> 00:34:21,092
I think I got something.

458
00:34:21,342 --> 00:34:24,804
Anita Doty, 33.
She's the ex-wife of Clyde's brother.

459
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:27,890
She has an arrest for check kiting.
Single, no dependents.

460
00:34:28,099 --> 00:34:30,851
- Clyde sent her money last month, $500.
- That's her.

461
00:34:31,435 --> 00:34:34,146
- Do we have an address?
- 225 B, Cedar Street, in Hayward.

462
00:34:34,730 --> 00:34:36,440
All right,
if we can find her, so can Volker.

463
00:34:36,566 --> 00:34:37,817
Cho, Rigsby, let's go.

464
00:34:38,109 --> 00:34:39,151
Yeah, right behind you.

465
00:34:46,784 --> 00:34:49,954
It's apartment B.
Upstairs.

466
00:34:53,583 --> 00:34:57,336
- What's this?
- It's the job.

467
00:35:01,757 --> 00:35:02,800
What do you want me to do with him?

468
00:35:05,303 --> 00:35:06,345
What do you think?

469
00:35:07,305 --> 00:35:09,307
- I can't do that.
- What do you mean?

470
00:35:10,141 --> 00:35:13,728
- Get up there now.
- No. Sorry. No kids.

471
00:35:14,437 --> 00:35:16,272
Never killed a kid. I'm not starting now.

472
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:22,862
I will bury you for this. You hear me?

473
00:35:24,614 --> 00:35:27,783
You do what you have to.
But I'm not killing a little kid.

474
00:37:02,169 --> 00:37:04,422
- Hey, Cho, what's up?
- "We're at the apartment."

475
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:07,341
No one's here. But the door's broken open.
There are signs of a struggle.

476
00:37:07,925 --> 00:37:10,386
- Do you think he took Marvin?
- Can't be sure.

477
00:37:11,095 --> 00:37:12,138
Damn it.

478
00:37:19,270 --> 00:37:20,312
Cho.

479
00:37:21,397 --> 00:37:22,815
- Hang on a second.
- Check this out.

480
00:37:27,069 --> 00:37:28,738
- Boss, I don't think Volker has him.
- Why?

481
00:37:29,405 --> 00:37:31,449
Because Marvin's on a field trip.
He's at the city zoo.

482
00:37:32,199 --> 00:37:34,201
Get Oakland P.D. there.
We're on our way.

483
00:37:49,300 --> 00:37:50,342
Hey, Marvin?

484
00:37:51,802 --> 00:37:52,845
Marvin Pettigrew?

485
00:38:15,284 --> 00:38:16,327
I'm with her.

486
00:38:16,744 --> 00:38:18,621
- Do you see him?
- No.

487
00:38:53,030 --> 00:38:54,073
Marvin?

488
00:38:55,783 --> 00:38:56,826
Marvin Pettigrew?

489
00:39:04,250 --> 00:39:05,292
It's...

490
00:39:06,335 --> 00:39:08,045
It's okay. I need you
to come with me, Marvin.

491
00:39:08,170 --> 00:39:09,505
I'm gonna take you to see your mother.

492
00:39:10,297 --> 00:39:12,550
But Anita said
that my mother was dead.

493
00:39:13,175 --> 00:39:15,219
No, no, that's not true.

494
00:39:16,011 --> 00:39:18,764
I'm gonna take you to see her.
Just come with me.

495
00:39:20,474 --> 00:39:21,517
Come with me, Marvin.

496
00:39:23,352 --> 00:39:24,395
Come here.

497
00:39:24,728 --> 00:39:26,188
- Let go of me.
- Come on, kid.

498
00:39:26,355 --> 00:39:27,648
- Let go...
- Shut up.

499
00:39:32,111 --> 00:39:33,279
"Let go. Help!"

500
00:39:33,821 --> 00:39:36,365
- It's Volker. He's here.
- "Help!"

501
00:39:45,624 --> 00:39:47,710
- Help! Help!
- Shut up, kid, shut up!

502
00:39:47,835 --> 00:39:49,628
- Hey! What you doing?
- He's taking me!

503
00:39:49,753 --> 00:39:52,298
Hey, let go of that kid!
Get him to stop!

504
00:39:52,590 --> 00:39:53,632
Hey.

505
00:40:03,559 --> 00:40:04,602
Drop it!

506
00:40:07,855 --> 00:40:08,898
Lisbon, you all right?

507
00:40:09,023 --> 00:40:11,108
- Yeah, I'm all right.
- I'm gonna find the kid.

508
00:40:11,775 --> 00:40:12,818
You're under arrest.

509
00:40:20,409 --> 00:40:22,453
Relax, Volker, it's over.

510
00:40:27,958 --> 00:40:30,669
- Call up dispatch.
- "We're heading over now."

511
00:40:49,229 --> 00:40:50,272
Be right there.

512
00:40:56,445 --> 00:40:57,696
- Marvin!
- Mom!

513
00:40:58,155 --> 00:41:00,616
Oh my God. Oh, God.

514
00:41:12,419 --> 00:41:13,462
Oh, God.
